Maros–Mészáros convex QP test set, small subset

The 48 problems in this directory with n + m <= 1000 (m counting every row of A, bound rows
included) come from https://github.com/qpsolvers/maros_meszaros_qpbenchmark, directory data/, at
commit c7d02f4f3a27e26fc5c248fe8366e2d0b87a6de0 (2024-01-17), distributed under the Apache License
2.0 (LICENSE in this directory). The original test set is described in

  I. Maros and C. Mészáros, A repository of convex quadratic programming problems,
  Optimization Methods and Software 11(1-4), 671-681, 1999. doi:10.1080/10556789908805768

Modification: each .mat file was converted to a compressed .npz with the same fields (P and A in
CSC form, q, r, l, u); no values were changed. The problems read

  minimize 1/2 x^T P x + q^T x + r   subject to   l <= A x <= u,

with P stored in full (both triangles) and +-1e20 (sometimes rounded to 9.999999999999998e19)
standing for an infinite bound. The loader, _problem in
tests/integration/test_sparse_kkt.py, splits equality, inequality and bound rows
for the interior-point method's regularized systems.

The problem archives above are unchanged copies from origin/devrush at the same basename.
The added *_patterns.npz files are reference results, generated from the frozen branch's
src/scaly/opt/ipm/kkt.py::Kernels.kkt_matrix, the corresponding full regularized system,
and src/scaly/ad/sparsity.py::jacobian_sparsity. The source is read
through git show; no devrush implementation is ported. Fields record both KKT patterns and
their value Jacobians in CSC order, and the P, A, G,
A-transpose and G-transpose product Jacobians with respect to the vector and matrix data.
The P data contains its upper triangle, shared by the mirrored off-diagonal coordinates.
Regularization entries and matrix values are independent symbolic parameters.

The test rewrites that problem against main's public API and recomputes numerical references
with SciPy and central differences. It follows devrush's equality/inequality/bound row split.
